    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mullery O’Gara are pleased to present 58 Sandford Road to the open market. An exceptional, deceptively spacious Victorian red brick period house, c. 2012  Sq.Ft  / 187 Sq.M.\r\n\r\nElegantly proportioned throughout, full of natural light, kitchen and interior architecture by Roisin Lafferty, and extended to rear. Carefully maintained by its present owners, retaining original features and the benefit of vehicular access/parking to rear approached from Marlborough Road.\r\n\r\nSecluded front garden, designed by Marion Keogh, bordered by mature hedging and well stocked with a variety of shrubs and box hedging. The rear garden is paved with Italian stone and features an attractive cut stone boundary wall in sandstone. \r\n\r\nThe accommodation is full of warmth with notable floor to ceiling heights and generous room proportions. It includes Hall with original ceiling cornice and centre roses, understairs cloak area. Interconnected reception rooms are generously proportioned with extra height ceilings.  Reception Room 1 has been plumbed for a gas fire, marble mantlepiece, original ceiling cornice and centre rose, integrated alcove units, door to Reception Room 2, which has  large wood-fired stove and ornate cast iron mantlepiece, , ceiling cornice and centre rose, steps to large open plan Roisin Lafferty designed Kitchen/Dining room with extensive range of units, Belfast sink, timber and tiled floor, brick exposed wall. There is a pantry and a laundry room off, a w.c. and whb.\r\n\r\nOn the first-floor return is a spacious suite comprising Bedroom 1, a private bathroom and a spacious Study/walk in wardrobe.\r\n\r\nOn the first floor Bedroom 2 (Rear) has ornate cast iron mantlepiece and open fireplace, ceiling cornice, alcove unit, attractively fitted wardrobes. Master suite/Front (Bedroom 3) spans the width of the house and has 2 x windows overlooking Sandford Parish church to front. \r\n\r\nOn the second-floor return is Family/Main Bathroom with standalone roll-top cast iron bath, separate subway-tiled power shower, w.c., whb, spacious hot press.\r\n\r\nOn the second floor is Bedroom 4 with 3x Velux windows.\r\n\r\nThis property is wonderfully positioned beside Ranelagh and Donnybrook villages with nearby selection of shops, restaurants, cafes, beside bus routes, Luas and a host of schools including Sandford National, Ranelagh Multi-denominational, Scoil Bhride, Sandford Park, Gonzaga, Muckross Park, Alexandra College etc.\r\n\r\nThere are numerous sports facilities in the area, and the property is within walking distance of Herbert Park."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall\r\nCeiling cornice and centre roses. Stained timber floor. Understairs cloaks area and storage.\r\n\r\nReception Room 1 \r\nMarble mantlepiece with cast iron inset and fireplace plumbed for gas. Custom built Alcove cupboards and shelving. Ceiling cornice and centre rose. Picture rail. Double doors to:\r\n\r\nReception Room 2 \r\nOrnate cast iron mantlepiece. Large wood-fired stove. Bespoke alcove shelving. Ceiling cornice and centre rose. Picture rail. Stained timber floor.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining\r\nExtensive range of wall and floor units. Belfast sink with brass taps and attractive overhead glass light fixtures, plumbed for dishwasher. Timber and tiled floor. Part-tiled splashbacks. Recessed cupboard and ceiling lights. Dolphin’s Barn exposed brick wall, attractive wall and over-dining feature lighting and with kitchen-length skylight. Floor to ceiling timber framed cantilevered glass door to rear.\r\n\r\nPantry \r\nPlumbed for washing machine/and or pantry use. Tiled floors. Recessed lighting. Suitable for pantry shelving. \r\n\r\nLaundry Room\r\nplumbed for washing machine. Tiled floors. Recessed lighting. G.F.C.H Boiler.\r\n\r\nDownstairs WC\r\nW. C, whb with medicine cupboard. Tiled floor.\r\n\r\n\r\nFirst Floor Return – Suite \r\nEnsuite Shower-room\r\nPower shower, w.c., whb. Part tiled. Black and white tiled floor.\r\n\r\nHome Office/Study/Walk-In Wardrobe\r\nSpacious home office/workstation also suitable as walk in wardrobe. \r\n\r\nBedroom 1\r\nSteps lead down to rear-facing bedroom, 2x Velux windows.\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\nBedroom 2 (Rear)\r\nOrnate cast-iron mantlepiece. Ceiling cornice. Custom-f fitted wardrobe. Alcove cupboard and shelving.\r\n\r\nMaster Suite/Bedroom 3 Front)\r\nGenerously proportioned, floor to ceiling extra height Master Suite with 2 x Windows overlooking Sandford Parish Church to front.\r\n\r\n\r\nSecond Floor Return\r\nL shaped landing area. \r\n\r\nFamily/Main Bathroom\r\nStand-alone roll-top cast-iron bath, w.c., whb, stand-alone tiled power shower. Towel radiator. Stained timber floor. 2x Velux windows, Hot press and airing cupboard.\r\n\r\nSecond Floor\r\nBedroom 4\r\n3x Velux windows. Recessed lights.\r\n\r\nOutside\r\nFront\r\nPrivate front garden. Bordered by raised hedging with a variety of plants and shrubs. Box hedging.\r\n\r\nRear \r\nItalian stone tiled paving, parking for one vehicle, cut sandstone boundary wall. Bi-folding timber double doors leading to additional parking on Marlborough Road."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "C. 2012 Sq.Ft / 187 Sq.M\r\nGFCH\r\nRear vehicular access and private off-street parking \r\nAdditional parking by residential permit on Marlborough Road\r\nBeside Ranelagh village and adjacent to Donnybrook village, multiple bus routes and Luas\r\nShort stroll to Herbert Park and close to notable sports facilities including David Lloyd, Dublin Riverview, Mount Pleasant and Fitzwilliam Tennis Clubs, as well the conveniences of two villages – Ranelagh and Donnybrook. \r\nEasy access to Dublin 2 and City Centre by walking, cycling, Luas and bus."
      },
